# rig_from_charset_op settings (BOOK 16.game/BOX-LIMB-RIG-FOR-WALKING-CHARACTERS-2026-11-25.md). Fractions are of the figure's opaque bounding-box height, top = 0.
# CONVERT | key | value
CONVERT | head_end | 0.56
CONVERT | torso_end | 0.84
CONVERT | hair_top_frac | 0.40
CONVERT | hair_side_frac | 0.18
CONVERT | skin_band_lo | 0.40
CONVERT | skin_band_hi | 0.85
CONVERT | eye_band_lo | 0.40
CONVERT | eye_band_hi | 0.85
CONVERT | sleeve_side_frac | 0.22
CONVERT | shoe_frac | 0.15
CONVERT | alpha_min | 128
CONVERT | outline_max | 24
CONVERT | same_colour_dist | 40
CONVERT | quant_shift | 3
# Profile mode (chibi sheets, 2026-11-25): the face is the first band of skin-hued pixels, the head ends under the chin, torso and legs split the rest of the body.
# A skin pixel has red >= skin_r_min and green / red in [skin_g_lo, skin_g_hi], blue / red in [skin_b_lo, skin_b_hi]. Without profile_mode the fixed fractions above apply.
CONVERT | profile_mode | 1
CONVERT | skin_r_min | 150
CONVERT | skin_g_lo | 0.62
CONVERT | skin_g_hi | 0.92
CONVERT | skin_b_lo | 0.45
CONVERT | skin_b_hi | 0.85
CONVERT | body_torso_frac | 0.5
CONVERT | chin_min_px | 3
# Skin settings (2026-11-25, polish): how a Minecraft-style skin cell is sampled from the sprite (rig_from_charset_op writes <rig>.skin.csv). All optional; a file without them keeps the plain average.
# skin_mode 1 = dominant colour of the cell (flat areas stay flat); skin_quant = bucket coarseness 3..6; skin_detail_frac / skin_detail_dist = a distinct minority (an eye, a mouth) wins when it covers that
# fraction of the cell and differs by more than the distance; skin_outline_frac = a cell that is at least this fraction dark outline becomes outline (crisp edges, 0 = off); skin_darken = shade the side and bottom faces (0 = off).
CONVERT | skin_mode | 1
CONVERT | skin_quant | 4
CONVERT | skin_detail_frac | 0.50
CONVERT | skin_detail_dist | 90
CONVERT | skin_outline_frac | 0.95
CONVERT | skin_darken | 0.10
CONVERT | skin_limb_rows | 1
CONVERT | skin_hand_rows | 2
